<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The release build has isShrinkResources on, and the shrinker took the alarm clip out
    of version 1.6 entirely. The id stayed in resources.arsc, so the URI still built and
    still pointed somewhere - it pointed at nothing, and MediaPlayer threw
    "Prepare failed.: status=0x1" with no other clue.

    The reference is a plain R.raw in Kotlin and should have been enough. It was not, and
    a resource the app cannot run without is not something to leave to inference.

    Measured rather than assumed: unzip the released APK and look for res/raw. If the mp3
    is missing, this file is not doing its job.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@raw/jarvis_neutralize" />
